  "description": "Erection of single storey outbuilding within rear garden. \r\r1. Dimensions and Siting: The building has a rectangular footprint of 4.80 metres in width and 3.00 metres in depth (14.4m \r2 ). It is sited in the rear garden, positioned 0.5 metres from the boundary shared with a row of single-storey garages. The maximum height of the building is 2.49 metres at the ridge, complying with the 2.5-metre height limit for structures within 2 metres of a boundary.\r\r2. Access and Layout: No new or altered vehicle or pedestrian access to the highway is proposed.\r\r3. Hard-standing: The building is situated on a dedicated level base. Total building coverage remains well below 50% of the garden curtilage.\r\r4. Means of Enclosure: No new fences or walls are proposed. The existing boundary remains a row of single-storey, windowless garages.\r\r5. Drainage: The roof is designed with a natural drip-edge; rainwater sheds directly onto the permeable garden ground within the applicant's property boundaries, ensuring natural infiltration.",
